From 7dfede434152ca39a2e04613ff9ed8b6c185a70a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:22:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dialog, popover: top layer, close watchers and the Popover
 API

The document now keeps a top layer, the showing auto popover list, the open
dialogs list and a close watcher manager (document/top_layer.rs).

Dialogs: showModal() adds the dialog to the top layer and close() removes
it; open dialogs get a close watcher, so an Escape keydown the page does not
cancel fires cancel and then close on the topmost modal dialog, as in
Chrome. requestClose(), closedBy and the request-close command are
implemented, and closedby=any dialogs close on a click outside of them.
Content outside the topmost modal dialog is inert: it is not focusable and
gets no mouse events.

Popovers: showPopover(), hidePopover(), togglePopover(), the popover
attribute, popovertarget/popovertargetaction on buttons and inputs, the
toggle-/show-/hide-popover commands, beforetoggle and coalesced toggle
events, auto popover stacking and light dismiss (click outside, Escape).
Hint popovers share the auto stack instead of a separate hint list.

History-action activation is tracked on the window so that a close request
may only be cancelled once per user activation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
